{
 "_doc": "How the men hold their arms and the rifle. 'hang' is the arms at rest, swinging as they walk (Creel needs it). 'rifle' is the swallow-tail rifle carried on the right shoulder, muzzle up and back, and brought up to aim: the butt in the shoulder, the left hand under the barrel, a kick back as it fires. 'rifle_up' and 'ram_high'/'ram_low' are the reload: the rifle stood upright, held by the barrel, and the rod driven down it (src/smyana/men_view.lobster bakes these poses). Places are in arm lengths from the shoulder: x to his right, y ahead, z up. The rifle's model (models/rifle_swallow_tail.vox, a copy of art/men/vox/gear/) is 66 voxels long, butt to muzzle along its y; the hand holds the wrist of the stock, 18 voxels from the butt. (2026-11-12, Dominic: the barrel looked \"almost like a hand cannon\": the barrel's and stock's capsules halved, iron 0.32 to 0.16 and wood 0.42 to 0.22.)",
